&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


  Synchronizing React Cart State with the Native MainButton
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The most common bug in Mini App shops is the "stale click listener" on the &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt;. Because the &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; is a singleton outside the React component tree, attaching a click listener inside a component that re-renders will either bind multiple instances of the listener or capture stale state variables in a closure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To prevent this, we must use a dedicated &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; hook that synchronizes the cart state with the &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; visibility, text, and active state, and cleanly removes the event listener on cleanup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is our &lt;code&gt;ProductCatalog.tsx&lt;/code&gt; component:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
